\ ---- SI units and basic currencies ----
\ Dimensioned quantities (see the reference). Names are spelled out and
\ lowercase: a capital symbol like N or A would shadow the capital-letter
\ logic-var convention. Each currency is its own dimension: the major unit is
\ the base, the minor unit 1/100 of it.

base unit m
base unit s
base unit kg
base unit ampere
base unit kelvin
base unit mol

1 1 s / unit hertz
1 kg 1 m * 1 s / 1 s / unit newton
1 newton 1 m / 1 m / unit pascal
1 newton 1 m * unit joule
1 joule 1 s / unit watt
1 ampere 1 s * unit coulomb
1 watt 1 ampere / unit volt

60 s unit minute
3600 s unit hour
86400 s unit day
7 day unit week

\ wall-clock time: epoch seconds as a quantity in s
: wall-now ( -- instant ) (wall-now) s ;
inline

\ { :year :month :day :hour :minute :second :weekday :yearday }, UTC
: epoch>date ( instant -- date ) 1 s / (epoch>date) ;
inline

\ :year required; :month :day default 1, clock fields 0; UTC
: date>epoch ( date -- instant ) (date>epoch) s ;
inline

\ epoch>date in the process's local timezone
: epoch>date-local ( instant -- date ) 1 s / (epoch>date-local) ;
inline

\ date>epoch in the process's local timezone; mktime resolves DST
: date>epoch-local ( date -- instant ) (date>epoch-local) s ;
inline

\ render an instant with strftime, UTC
: format-time ( instant format -- string ) swap 1 s / swap (format-time) ;
inline

\ render an instant with strftime in the local timezone
: format-time-local ( instant format -- string ) swap 1 s / swap (format-time-local) ;
inline

\ parse with strptime; unmatched fields default to 1970-01-01
\ 00:00:00, read as UTC unless the format captures an offset with %z
: parse-time ( string format -- instant ) (parse-time) s ;
inline

\ ISO 8601 in UTC: 2026-07-09T12:34:56Z
: time>iso ( instant -- string ) "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" format-time ;
inline

\ parse the ISO 8601 Z form time>iso emits
: iso>time ( string -- instant ) "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" parse-time ;
inline

: days-in-month ( year month -- days )
	| y m |
	{ :year y :month m 1 + } date>epoch
	{ :year y :month m } date>epoch
	- 1 day / ;

\ calendar shift, UTC: :years :months step the
\ calendar with the day clamped to the target month; :weeks :days :hours
\ :minutes :seconds add exactly
: date-shift ( instant delta -- instant )
	| instant delta |

	delta :years 0 @or 12 *
	delta :months 0 @or + to months
	
	months 0= not if
		instant epoch>date to date
		date@year 12 * date@month + 1- months + to months
		months 12 quotient to year
		months 12 mod 1+ to month
		year month days-in-month to day-of-month
		date@day day-of-month < if date@day to day-of-month then

		{ 
		  :year year 
		  :month month 
		  :day day-of-month
		  :hour date@hour 
		  :minute date@minute
		  :second date@second 
		} date>epoch to instant
	then
	
	instant
	delta :weeks 0 @or week +
	delta :days 0 @or day +
	delta :hours 0 @or hour +
	delta :minutes 0 @or minute +
	delta :seconds 0 @or s + ;

1000 m unit km

base unit $ 1 $ 100 / unit ¢
base unit £ 1 £ 100 / unit penny
base unit € 1 € 100 / unit eurocent

\ data (IEC binary units, powers of 1024); MiB is the base, so B is 1/2^20 MiB
\ and PiB is 2^30 MiB
base unit MiB
1 MiB 1024 / unit KiB
1 KiB 1024 / unit B
1024 MiB unit GiB
1024 GiB unit TiB
1024 TiB unit PiB

\ re-express q in the unit that unit-xt attaches (' MiB)
: as ( q unit-xt -- q' ) | q unit-xt | 1 unit-xt execute 0 * q + ;
